{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-28 03:53:51 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 10:53:51 ICT\n\nThe r9 envelope fix is present: lift carries the original envelope, and lower uses it directly as `:datom` ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:345), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:635)). The added pins cover the extra `:producer/nonce` key through round-trip and real-engine retry ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:513), [remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:992)).\n\nOne requirement remains unmet. For an envelope-less `:ffi-request`, `lower-frame` calls `attach-all` **before** `lower-one` checks for the envelope ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:716), [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:640)). The refusal test verifies the eventual status and request identity, but does not establish refusal before stream resolution ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:1271)). This gate explicitly requires that ordering. I did not edit files or rerun suites.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
